N2  - Purpose: The purpose of the study is to investigate the meridian. Methods: After the patients accepted arthroscopic repair for triangular fibrocartilage complex (TFCC) tears, the investigator use electroacupuncture for postoperative pain relief. It is expected that 20 patients will be randomly assigned to the following groups: electroacupuncture group (EAG), EA at points; non-point group (NPG), EA at non-points. Acupoint selection: *true acupoints: needles were inserted to Kunlun (BL60) and Sanyinjiao (SP6) contralateral to the operated leg and deqi sensation elicited at acupoints *false point: the needles were inserted to Zusanli (ST36) and Shangjuxu (ST37) contralateral to the operated leg and deqi sensation elicited at acupoints Data collection: the investigator recorded the data including the time required for the first injection of analgesics and the number of doses of injection painkiller used in 24 hours after surgery (count). Results: The group of electroacupuncture group (EAG) significant increases in the time required for the first injection of analgesics and drease in the number of doses of injection painkiller than the group of non-point group (NPG). Conclusion: We think electroacupuncture group (EAG) is effective because the meridian is right.
