N2  - The authors report on studies of electroacupuncture in 70 volunteers. They studied the pain threshold, the threshold of pain tolerance over the area of a planned operation. Reactions to electroacupuncture varied in different individuals. The role of neurophysiological mechanisms in the manifestation of analgetic action of the procedure is discussed. Its effect can be compared to that of morphine. The best results were seen in the combination of electroacupuncture and analgin.
